{"_id":"68a736128ec3d8323af147d5","roadmapSlug":"data-analyst","nodeId":"PqGO8AU1zE2ZdtqrIrOkZ","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:58.099Z","description":"# Kurtosis\n\nKurtosis measures the heaviness of a distribution's tails compared to a normal distribution. High kurtosis (leptokurtic) means more values in the tails and a sharper peak; low kurtosis (platykurtic) means thinner tails and a flatter peak. It is used alongside skewness to assess whether data approximates a normal distribution.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Kurtosis: Definition, Types, and Importance","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/k/kurtosis.asp","_id":"6a7f4a4fcb44947debcf5a00"},{"type":"video","title":"What is Kurtosis?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AsxEDBhESJg","_id":"6a7f4a4fcb44947debcf5a01"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:03:11.488Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a8894ecaca636c6b9e973f1","title":"DataCamp - Associate Data Analyst in SQL","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/1GK1qD"},{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d041675b","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/AgYmJK"},{"_id":"6a5e189a077863512aba4c73","title":"roadmap.sh - Master SQL","partner":"roadmap.sh","type":"course","url":"https://roadmap.sh/courses/sql"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/data-analyst/content/PqGO8AU1zE2ZdtqrIrOkZ.md"}